"""`api/agent/lessons.py`. `report_outcome` is a plain insert, tested against the row it leaves.
`retry_unsettled` is where every core-memory call happens: most tests fake `lessons.Client` and
`lessons.vend_envelope` so no real one is needed; two run against a real closed socket and a real
server that never answers, since a real fastmcp client wraps a connection fault as a bare
`RuntimeError` no monkeypatched exception type would ever surface.
"""

